# Sound branch (#349, D80): the branch skin of a one-way Platform, native 32x16. Joins a trunk on its left edge: its root
# (columns 0-2) swells by a row up and down into a dark bark collar that lies over the trunk's bark (D122);
# perch-left is the same branch on the left of a trunk. Active tier (D76): ink contour, living bark in lengthwise streaks
# with a knot, a pale walkable top line (the log's "stand here" line), tapering to a green leaf tuft at its tip; nothing
# hangs under its middle (#556: that read as an animal's leg). No crack, no grey: those mean a rotten branch.
# Leaf tuft (#594, 2026-11-27): dark leaves with pale moonlit tips `T` on top, so the tuft keeps a clear contrast margin
# against both the moon and the dark sky. `G` is darker than the moon rim's SOURCE_L, so the export also rims the `G` pixels on
# a lit edge in `c4cfe8` (five a frame), as in the sheet the author approved.
# Joint (D130, 2026-11-24): the collar is the trunk's red-brown bark (1 2 3 4) and the root (columns 0-6) ramps into it through a
# half step (5 6 7); keys 1-7 are kept out of the moon rim.
size 32 16
color k 0b0814
color W 4a2e1c
color w 8a5a30
color l c08a4c
color g 2f5a2c
color G 3a5e22
color T c4e89a
color 1 47302a
color 2 2e1813
color 3 28130e
color 4 220e09
color 5 815b3c
color 6 5a3722
color 7 392015
frame perch
